  "concept": "strings: split, indexing, upper() and building a result in a loop",
  "task": "Write a function `initials(full_name)` that returns the initials of a name in capital letters, each followed by a dot.\nSplit the name into words, take the first letter of each word, make it upper-case and add a `.` after it.\nExample: `initials('Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar')` returns `'S.R.T.'` and `initials('mithali raj')` returns `'M.R.'`.\nExtra spaces must not matter: `initials('  virat   kohli ')` is `'V.K.'`, and an empty string gives `''`.",
  "starter": "def initials(full_name):\n    \"\"\"Return initials like 'S.R.T.' for 'Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar'.\"\"\"\n    # 1. split the name into a list of words\n    # 2. for each word take the first letter, make it upper-case, add '.'\n    # 3. return the combined string\n    pass\n\n# Try it: change the name and press Run\nprint(initials(\"Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar\"))   # should print S.R.T.\n",
  "solution": "def initials(full_name):\n    \"\"\"Return initials like 'S.R.T.' for 'Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar'.\"\"\"\n    words = full_name.split()   # split() with no argument also throws away extra spaces\n    result = \"\"\n    for word in words:\n        result += word[0].upper() + \".\"\n    return result\n\n# Try it: change the name and press Run\nprint(initials(\"Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar\"))   # S.R.T.\n",
  "tests": "check(\"initials('Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar') returns 'S.R.T.'\", lambda: initials('Sachin Ramesh Tendulkar') == 'S.R.T.', \"Use full_name.split() to get the words, then take word[0] from each.\")\ncheck(\"lower-case names are capitalised: 'mithali raj' gives 'M.R.'\", lambda: initials('mithali raj') == 'M.R.', \"Call .upper() on each first letter.\")\ncheck(\"extra spaces are ignored: '  virat   kohli ' gives 'V.K.'\", lambda: initials('  virat   kohli ') == 'V.K.', \"split() with NO argument splits on any amount of spaces; split(' ') does not.\")\ncheck(\"a single name works: 'Dhoni' gives 'D.'\", lambda: initials('Dhoni') == 'D.', \"Every initial, even the last one, is followed by a dot.\")\ncheck(\"an empty name gives an empty string ''\", lambda: initials('') == '', \"Start with result = '' and only add to it inside the loop.\")",
